The [[Hero Longsword]] is a neutral [[weapon]] normally only obtainable by combining a [[Hero Sword]] with two [[Whetstone]]s. It is a much upgraded [[Hero Sword]], dealing much more damage and granting much more damage to the adjacent weapons. Its only drawbacks over the [[Hero Sword]] are its larger size and using slightly more stamina, but it does also have more sockets and {{icon/star}} slots.

There are two subsequent upgrades for the [[Hero Longsword]]:

By combining the [[Hero Longsword]] with the [[Falcon Blade]]s, the [[Crossblades]] can be created, which is a powerful +-shaped weapon which grants a large amount of damage to one weapon and massively speeds up another item. It also deals more damage and attacks faster with every hit.

By combining the [[Hero Longsword]] with two [[Flame]]s (which are easily obtainable by [[Pyromancer]]s, and consistently obtainable by [[Berserker]]s if they select the [[Anvil]] as their subclass item), the [[Burning Blade]] can be created, which is a more {{icon/heat}} themed version of the [[Hero Longsword]], likely dealing more damage than the [[Hero Longsword]] in a build capable of generating lots of {{icon/heat}}, but probably weaker otherwise.
